siao-k%27o\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Y\u00fc Hsiao-k&#39;o\">Y\u00fc Hsiao-k'o</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu_Zhiding\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Yu Zhiding\">Wikipedia article</a>, <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367961\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367961\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3678433</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 2 \u2014 Y\u00fc Chih-ting</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">Tu Lien-ch\u00ea</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"941\" data-page-number=\"941\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 2.pdf/339\" data-page-index=\"339\" data-page-quality=\"3\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;2.pdf/339\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;339\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>Y\u00dc</b> Chih-ting \u79b9\u4e4b\u9f0e (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u5c1a\u5409, \u5c1a\u57fa, \u4e0a\u5409,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u613c\u9f4b), 1649\u20131702, painter, was a native of Chiang-tu, Kiangsu. In his youth he was a pupil of Lan Ying \u85cd\u745b (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u7530\u53d4,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u8776\u53df, \u77f3\u982d\u9640), a noted painter of the late Ming period. Y\u00fc Chih-ting's greatest skill lay in portraiture for which he generally used the so-called \"black and white\" method (\u767d\u83d7). He also employed the \"orchid leaf style\" (\u862d\u8449\u6cd5) of the great T'ang artist, Wu Tao-hs\u00fcan \u5433\u9053\u7384 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u9053\u5b50,&#32;early 8th century). For more than six years prior to 1690 he held a post in the capital as usher in the Court of State Ceremonial and also served in the Imperial Court as a painter. Many contemporaries of note, such as <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Wu_Wei-yeh\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Wu Wei-yeh\">Wu Wei-yeh</a></span>, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ch%27%C3%AAn_T%27ing-ching\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;\u00ean T&#39;ing-ching\">Ch'\u00ean T'ing-ching</a></span>, <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Kao_Shih-ch%27i\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Kao Shih-ch&#39;i\">Kao Shih-ch'i</a></span>, and <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Hs%C3%BC_Ch%27ien-hs%C3%BCeh\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Hs\u00fc Ch&#39;ien-hs\u00fceh\">Hs\u00fc Ch'ien-hs\u00fceh</a></span>&#32;[<i>qq.&#8239;v.</i>], induced him to prepare portraits and other paintings for them. In 1645 he retired from office, making his home at Tung-t'ing shan in T'ai-hu, Kiangsu. A painting by him, entitled \u738b\u6703\u5716 <i>Wang-hui t'u</i>, \"Assembly of the Princes\", was inspired by the chapter, <i>Wang-hui</i>, in the ancient work \u9038\u5468\u66f8 <i>I Chou-shu</i>. He presumably adapted it to the ceremonies then accorded by the Ch'ing Court to princes and ambassadors of tributary states. A painting which he made for <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Wang_Shih-ch%C3%AAn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Wang Shih-ch\u00ean\">Wang Shih-ch\u00ean</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] in 1701, entitled \u738b\u6f01\u6d0b\u8e0f\u96ea\u5c0b\u6885\u5716 <i>Wang Yu-yang t'a-hs\u00fceh hs\u00fcn-mei t'u</i>, is reproduced in the work, \u4e2d\u570b\u540d\u756b <i>Chung-kuo ming-hua</i>, series eight. The \u6545\u5bae\u9031\u520a <i>Ku-kung chou-k'an</i> (nos. 172 and 474) has also reproduced two of his paintings from the Palace Museum, Peiping.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[1/509/2b; 19/2\u4e0a/47b; 20/1/00 (portrait); 27/13/7b; <i>Chiang-tu hsien hs\u00fc-chih</i> (1831) 6/23a; Waley, <i>Index</i>, p. 109; <i>T'oung Pao</i> 1922, p. 359; Chavannes, <i>Ars Asiatica</i> I, p. 55; L.T.C.L.H.M., p. 191 lists a number of paintings attributed to him.]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">Tu Lien-ch\u00ea</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00ean T'ing-ching"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Hs\u00fc Ch'ien-hs\u00fceh"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Kao Shih-ch'i"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wang Shih-ch\u00ean"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Wu Wei-yeh"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Y\u00fc-ch'ien"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Y\u00fc Hsiao-k'o"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Tu Lien-ch\u00ea"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 2\n | onlysection = yu chih-ting\n | previous = Y\u00fc-ch'ien\n | next     = Y\u00fc Hsiao-k'o\n | from     = 339\n | to       = 339\n | notes    =\n | section_author = Tu Lien-ch\u00ea\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Y\u00fc Chih-ting}}"}}}